    "reviewed_findings": [
      "The main page and seven variant pages use the accepted canonical player content. The trigger is a same-weapon melee kill; a killing hit resolves before the kill event and cannot retroactively use the new layer.",
      "All seven actual trait variants and seventeen actual bindings match the canonical config, shared map, and reverse weapon indexes; each own I–IV value is .05/.06/.07/.08 power_level_modifier per effective layer.",
      "The shared child structure has one zero-effective placeholder and up to five effective layers. The fallback .20 is overridden by each own same-key value; the shared 4.5-second timer refreshes at cap, expiry removes the effective layers, and held-slot conditions gate the trigger/stat as documented.",
      "The RAW EN/ZH templates are paired to the verified key/hash and reconstruct to +5/+6/+7/+8% Strength, 4.5 seconds, and five stacks. Formatter and localization comparison distinguish the raw text from runtime trigger restrictions.",
      "The formula and examples use the post-power-type-curve input and additive modifier pool: IV at five stacks changes 500 to 700 when q=0; with q=.20 it changes 600 to 800, a 33.33% relative input increase. Neither case claims a fixed final health-damage increase.",
      "Pure push and Force Sword P1 fling cannot create layers. Existing generic power can still affect push/fling impact calculations under the held/cache conditions; health damage is zero on those paths, and shield fixed-stagger overrides limit outcomes.",
      "Powermaul direct powered sweeps can qualify for a layer; its separate explosion attack cannot create one, though a previously cached held layer may affect it. The pages do not claim same-action newly gained layers already affect the blast.",
      "Thunderhammer powered hits remain direct melee; gibbing_type=explosion is not a separate explosion Attack. Icon URL, reverse indexes, map relation, source links, and focused checks are consistent with the actual seven variants/seventeen bindings."
    ],
